          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Clematis recta, the erect climaxis or ground virgins, is a species of Clematis unusual in that it is a free-standing shrub rather than a climbing plant. Growing usually on the margins of woodland areas, it is native to Eastern, Southern and Mid Europe."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Two varieties are accepted:\n{{species list\n|Clematis erecta nothovar. hybrida |Lemoine ex Bonard\n|Clematis erecta var. erecta|\n}}"
          }
        ]
      }
